  "notes": [
    "GPU0/1 occupied by unrelated services. Only free GPU3 A100-PCIE used.",
    "Simulated far and near are separate same-GPU HBM allocations, not physical NVLink. Unchanged emulator charges the same bytes and latency. Physical Host cases use normal builds.",
    "The two-version controlled baseline uses the same tiers.py same-device access-list fix.",
    "Profile patches and timestamp traces are diagnostic, never final timing evidence.",
    "16-row fetch ring regressed. The 32-row compact fetch ring regressed 15% on one zero-latency case. It is only in saved experimental patches, absent from the retained kernel.",
    "final_* files measure the pipeline candidate; accepted_* and retained_* measure intermediate candidates. An apparent recovery after isolating helpers did not persist; accepted/retained kernel instruction text was identical. No claim that isolation fixed the Host regression is supported.",
    "enabled_* and default_* compare the final explicit SMALL_PREPARE option with the original default. The option is disabled by default after a 6% Host timing regression in intermediate candidates.",
    "LRU ties within a launch may pick different victims, so reports preserve miss counts.",
    "All lower bounds use normal-build same-GPU pure-HBM samples; emulator floors are ignored."
  ]
